# Decimal separator in Russian documents

When generating or updating Russian-language documents (Word, Markdown, comments for the user, manuals in `docs/`), write the decimal separator as a period: `0.325`, `1.19`, `0.98`.

Do not use a comma as the decimal mark (`0,325`, `1,19`) except when quoting an OS/Excel locale string that literally contains a comma.
